{"game":"Grand Theft Auto VI","list":"the official 55 trophies, 2026-11-18","platform":"PlayStation 5","trophies":[{"description":"Congratulations! You're a Leonida Legend.","grade":"platinum","guide":"The platinum pops the moment the other 54 trophies are yours. There is no shortcut: it is the sum of the whole hunt. Expect around 200 to 300 hours in total, and remember the game has no difficulty trophies and no online trophies, so it is long rather than hard. Keep a manual save at the start of every chapter and one before the final mission, because there is no mission replay and no New Game Plus.","hidden":false,"id":1,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Vice Got a Price!","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"}],"stage":5,"steps":["Finish the story and every side strand first","Work the 100% Completion Checklist after the credits","Clean up the last activity and collectible trophies"]},{"description":"Complete Gone Fishing.","grade":"bronze","guide":"This is the opening mission, so it unlocks as you play through the start of the story. You cannot miss it: just follow the mission until the credits roll on it.","hidden":true,"id":2,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Just Like Paradise","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the opening mission, Gone Fishing, to its end"]},{"description":"Complete Chapter 1.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Chapter trophies unlock as the story moves on, so play through Chapter 1 and this one pops at its end. Before you leave Chapter 1, meditate at Lucia's balcony spot: it is the one meditation spot that disappears once the chapter ends, and it counts toward Positive Mental Attitude.","hidden":true,"id":3,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Paradise Lost","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Finish every mission in Chapter 1"]},{"description":"Complete Chapter 2.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Play through Chapter 2 to its end. Once the mission Coffee Break is done you can switch characters and call your partner, which opens up the partner trophies Hot Together and Retail Therapy.","hidden":true,"id":4,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"T**s Ass Drug Money","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"GTABase — GTA 6 Trophies & Achievements Guide","url":"https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-achievements-trophies-list-ps5-xbox-series"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Finish every mission in Chapter 2"]},{"description":"Complete Chapter 3.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Chapter 3's trophy pops when the last mission of the chapter is done. By now the robbery trophies start opening up, so keep an eye out for bank vaults and armored trucks while you play.","hidden":true,"id":5,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Vice City, Baby!","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Finish every mission in Chapter 3"]},{"description":"Complete Chapter 4.","grade":"bronze","guide":"The last chapter trophy before the finale. Finish Chapter 4 and this one is yours; the final mission trophy follows right after.","hidden":true,"id":6,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Top Of The World, Ma","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Finish every mission in Chapter 4"]},{"description":"Complete the final mission.","grade":"gold","guide":"The story's last mission. Save by hand before you start it, since there is no mission replay if you want to see it again. Once the credits roll you can keep exploring Leonida freely, and the 100% Completion Checklist unlocks for the cleanup.","hidden":true,"id":7,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"You Gotta Know When to Get Off","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the final mission to its end","Keep a manual save before you start it"]},{"description":"Complete Breakfast Run.","grade":"bronze","guide":"A story mission trophy: finish Breakfast Run and it pops. Mission trophies like this one cannot be missed as long as you play the story through.","hidden":true,"id":8,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Trust","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the mission Breakfast Run to its end"]},{"description":"Complete The Cartel Heist.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Finish the story mission The Cartel Heist. It is one of the big set-piece heists, and the trophy is automatic once the mission is complete.","hidden":true,"id":9,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Break the Bank","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the mission The Cartel Heist to its end"]},{"description":"Complete Child's Play.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Finish the story mission Child's Play. Like the other mission trophies, it unlocks on its own as you play the campaign.","hidden":true,"id":10,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Family Matters","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the mission Child's Play to its end"]},{"description":"Complete Headliners.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Finish the story mission Headliners. Another automatic story trophy: complete the mission and it is yours.","hidden":true,"id":11,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"DWNFALL","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the mission Headliners to its end"]},{"description":"Complete VCIA Takedown.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Finish the story mission VCIA Takedown at Vice City International Airport. The trophy pops when the mission ends, and the airport itself is worth remembering: you come back here later for the Catch Me If You Can trophy.","hidden":true,"id":12,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Hi-Jacked","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the mission VCIA Takedown to its end"]},{"description":"Complete Operation Savage Glory.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Finish the story mission Operation Savage Glory. It is the last of the named-mission trophies, and it unlocks the same way as the rest: complete the mission.","hidden":true,"id":13,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Snow Storm","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Exophase / PSNProfiles — official PSN trophy list"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the mission Operation Savage Glory to its end"]},{"description":"Attain 100% Completion.","grade":"gold","guide":"The big one. You do not have to do literally everything: the checklist asks for 15 of the 18 collectible card sets and 70 of the 80 challenges, among its other tasks. It only appears once the story is finished, so play the campaign first, then use the checklist as your cleanup list. Track it any time with Touch Pad, then Progress, then 100% Completion. Most of the other trophies fall out of this work on their own.","hidden":false,"id":14,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"A Long Road","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":5,"steps":["Finish the story to unlock the 100% Completion Checklist","Open it with Touch Pad, then Progress, then 100% Completion","Work the checklist: 15 of 18 card sets, 70 of 80 challenges, and the rest"]},
{"description":"Complete 250 Stunts.","grade":"silver","guide":"There are 397 stunts in the game, and you need 250 of them: 130 Stunt Jumps off ramps and bridges, 202 Under the Bridges flights, 40 Knife Flights between tall buildings, and 25 Base Jumps off the tallest peaks. You only need a little over half, so skip the ones that fight you. Find them on the map with Touch Pad, then Exploration, then Stunt Spots, and track progress with Touch Pad, then Progress, then Activities, then Stunts.","hidden":false,"id":15,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Cunning Stunts","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Open the map: Touch Pad, then Exploration, then Stunt Spots","Work the easy Stunt Jumps and Under the Bridges first","Track progress: Touch Pad, then Progress, then Activities, then Stunts"]},
{"description":"Try each type of activity once.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Try all nine activity types once: fishing, hunting, golf, a shooting range, pool, basketball (sink one basket), an arcade game, winning a race (a car race, a race challenge or a Top Fun drone race), and a stunt. Most of these happen naturally as you play, and Progress, then Activities shows you what is left. Do the odd ones out early, like sinking a basketball shot, so you do not have to hunt for them later.","hidden":false,"id":16,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Master of None","sources":[{"name":"GTABase — GTA 6 Trophies & Achievements Guide","url":"https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-achievements-trophies-list-ps5-xbox-series"},{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Try fishing, hunting, golf, a shooting range, pool and basketball","Finish an arcade game and win any race","Pull off any stunt, then check Progress, then Activities"]},
{"description":"Earn a gold medal in all Shooting Range challenges.","grade":"silver","guide":"Gold medals in all 42 Shooting Range challenges, across the two ranges: Rodgers Ranch & Shooting Range in Port Gellhorn and Griffin Shooting Range in Balsero. Most challenges have three difficulty tiers to gold, and some stay locked until you meet other conditions, which the map shows. Find the ranges with Touch Pad, then Activities, then Shooting Ranges, and track progress the same way.","hidden":false,"id":17,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"The Shootist","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Visit both ranges: Rodgers Ranch (Port Gellhorn) and Griffin (Balsero)","Gold each challenge through its three tiers","Check the map for locked challenges and their conditions"]},
{"description":"Win a Top Fun Drone Race at every location.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Win a Top Fun Drone Race at all 14 locations. Some of them charge an entry fee, so keep some cash on hand. The races are quick once you learn the lines, and losing one costs nothing but the fee. See every location on the map with Touch Pad, then Activities, then Drones, then Top Fun Drones.","hidden":false,"id":18,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Top Fun","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Find the races: Touch Pad, then Activities, then Drones, then Top Fun Drones","Win at each of the 14 locations","Bring cash: some locations charge an entry fee"]},
{"description":"Win 20 different races.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Win 20 different races. Repeating the same race does not count, so keep moving to new locations. Most race spots let you hire a car; if you bring your own, watch its Rating, which you can raise with upgrades from Mod Shops. Track them all with Touch Pad, then Activities, then Racing.","hidden":false,"id":19,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Earn Cash, Not Kudos","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Win a race at 20 different locations","Hire a car at the spot or upgrade your own at a Mod Shop","Track them: Touch Pad, then Activities, then Racing"]},
{"description":"Beat Cal in a fishing challenge.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Fairly early on, Cal asks you to catch a Parrotfish over 2kg. Take a boat with a fishing rod to the area marked on your map and fish there until you land one big enough. If you have no boat of your own, plenty are sitting around the area to borrow.","hidden":false,"id":20,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Baited My Tackle","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Wait for Cal's request to catch a Parrotfish over 2kg","Take a boat with a fishing rod to the marked area","Fish until you land one over 2kg and beat Cal"]},
{"description":"Complete an arcade game.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Finish any arcade game, start to end. Arcades are scattered around Vice City and the wider state; pick the game you find easiest and play it through. This also counts as one of the nine activity types for Master of None.","hidden":false,"id":21,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Stick Fiddler","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Find an arcade and pick any game","Play it through to completion"]},
{"description":"Complete the final mission for Andy.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Andy is one of the stranger characters with a mission strand of his own. Work through all of Andy's missions and this trophy pops when his last one is done. Stranger missions appear as you explore Leonida, so keep an eye on the map for their markers.","hidden":true,"id":22,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Road to Rehabilitation","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Find Andy's missions as you explore Leonida","Complete each one until his final mission"]},
{"description":"Complete the final mission for Kenton.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Kenton's strand ends with the mission Maritime Disputes. Finish that mission and the trophy is yours. Like the other stranger strands, his missions unlock as you explore, so do them when they appear rather than leaving them all for the end.","hidden":true,"id":23,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"This Was No Boat Accident","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Work through Kenton's missions","Complete his final mission, Maritime Disputes"]},
{"description":"Complete the final mission for Billy.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Billy's strand ends with the mission Hometown Heroes. Finish it and the trophy pops. Billy's missions are part of the stranger strands that also count toward Strangers & Freaks, so they pull double duty.","hidden":true,"id":24,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"The Lone Rider","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Work through Billy's missions","Complete his final mission, Hometown Heroes"]},
{"description":"Complete 8 mission strands for strangers across the state of Leonida.","grade":"silver","guide":"Finish eight full stranger mission strands across Leonida. The named strangers, Andy, Kenton, Billy, Randy and Tyrone, each have a strand of their own, and there are more strangers out in the state to find. Do their missions as you meet them; by the time the last strand is done, this silver pops alongside their individual trophies.","hidden":true,"id":25,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Strangers & Freaks","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Take every stranger mission you find while exploring","Finish 8 full strands, including Andy, Kenton, Billy, Randy and Tyrone"]},
{"description":"Complete the final mission for Randy.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Randy's strand ends with his final mission. His missions revolve around his Wish List of vehicles, so you will be hunting down specific cars for him along the way. Finish his last mission and the trophy pops.","hidden":true,"id":26,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Supply & Demand","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Work through Randy's missions and his Wish List vehicles","Complete his final mission"]},
{"description":"Complete the final mission for Tyrone.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Tyrone's strand ends with his final mission. His missions lead you to the Kitty Litter Lab locations, which help you progress his quest, so follow those markers when they show up. Finish his last mission and the trophy is yours.","hidden":true,"id":27,"kind":"story","missable":false,"name":"Spin On This!","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Work through Tyrone's missions","Use the Kitty Litter Lab locations to progress his quest","Complete his final mission"]},
{"description":"Meditate at every spot across Leonida.","grade":"bronze","guide":"There are 18 meditation spots across Leonida, and you must complete a meditation at each one. A meditation only counts once its final zen animation has played, so stay put until it finishes. Track them with Touch Pad, then Progress, then Collections, then Exploration, then Meditations, and find discovered spots on the map with Touch Pad, then Exploration, then Meditate Around Leonida. MISSABLE: Lucia's balcony meditation in Chapter 1 disappears after that chapter, so do it before you finish Chapter 1. There is no mission replay, so keep a manual save at the start of every chapter.","hidden":false,"id":28,"kind":"collectibles","missable":true,"name":"Positive Mental Attitude","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Meditate at Lucia's balcony spot BEFORE finishing Chapter 1","Meditate at all 18 spots; wait for the final zen animation each time","Track them: Touch Pad, then Progress, then Collections, then Exploration, then Meditations"]},
{"description":"Hunt a unique animal for Bret.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Bret wants a unique animal hunted down. Take on his hunting request and track the animal he names: unique animals are one-off hunts, not the regular wildlife, so follow his directions and the markers rather than wandering. Hunting also counts as one of the nine activity types for Master of None.","hidden":false,"id":29,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Fair Game","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Take Bret's hunting request","Track and hunt the unique animal he names"]},
{"description":"Complete 3 Collectible Card sets.","grade":"silver","guide":"There are 18 sets of Collectible Cards scattered around Leonida, and you need all the cards in 3 full sets. If you are going for 100% completion you will need 15 sets, so this trophy pops along the way. Cards you have collected can be sold at Pawn Shops and they still count toward your progress. Track them with Touch Pad, then Progress, then Collections, then Collectible Cards.","hidden":false,"id":30,"kind":"collectibles","missable":false,"name":"Don't Touch My Deck","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Collect every card in 3 full sets (15 sets for 100%)","Sell spare cards at Pawn Shops; they still count","Track them: Touch Pad, then Progress, then Collections, then Collectible Cards"]},
{"description":"WAiNK It at 100 locations.","grade":"silver","guide":"WAiNK is an app on Jason or Lucia's phone: hold Up to open it, then scan landmarks to learn more about them. There are 31 WAiNK landmarks, 35 curiosities and 23 sculptures to scan, plus No Flusher tags, and you need 100 successful scans in total. Scan everything you pass while you play and the count climbs on its own. Check progress with Touch Pad, then Progress, then Collections, then WAiNK Locations.","hidden":false,"id":31,"kind":"collectibles","missable":false,"name":"You WAiNKer!","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Open WAiNK on the phone (hold Up) and scan landmarks as you pass them","Scan 100 in total: landmarks, curiosities, sculptures and No Flusher tags","Track them: Touch Pad, then Progress, then Collections, then WAiNK Locations"]},
{"description":"Complete 50 Challenges.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Challenges are the game's in-world feats: there are 80 of them and you need 50. They cover skilled play across combat, driving, stunts and more, and 70 are needed for 100% completion, so this trophy pops on the way there. See every challenge and its requirement with Touch Pad, then Progress, then Challenges, and knock out the easy ones first.","hidden":false,"id":32,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"One Last Thing","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Open Touch Pad, then Progress, then Challenges","Complete 50 of the 80 challenges (70 for 100%)"]},
{"description":"Lose a 4 star Wanted Level with your partner and escape the heat.","grade":"bronze","guide":"This only opens up once both characters are together, after the Chapter 2 mission Coffee Break. Call your partner (hold Right on the D-pad, then Triangle or Y), build a 4-star Wanted Level, then escape until you are out of the red heat zone: it only counts once you have left it. The train tunnel north of Ambrosia in Kelly County shakes off cops and helicopters well. Bank vault robberies always bring 4 stars, so it often pops there on its own.","hidden":false,"id":33,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Hot Together","sources":[{"name":"GTABase — GTA 6 Trophies & Achievements Guide","url":"https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-achievements-trophies-list-ps5-xbox-series"},{"name":"egamers.io — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://egamers.io/gta-6-trophy-list-all-55-trophies-and-achievements-plus-the-hardest-ones/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Finish Coffee Break in Chapter 2 so both characters are together","Call your partner (hold Right on the D-pad, then Triangle or Y)","Reach a 4-star Wanted Level, then escape the red heat zone","The train tunnel north of Ambrosia in Kelly County works well"]},
{"description":"Rob 3 shops back-to-back with your partner without losing your Wanted Level.","grade":"bronze","guide":"With your partner beside you, rob three shops in a row while you are still wanted, shown by the flashing red and blue. The jewelry stores in north Vice City sit close together, which makes the run easy: take a few items in each shop, and blowing the back-room safe with sticky bombs helps it count. It pops a moment after you drive away from the third shop; if it does not, rob a fourth. This also opens up after Coffee Break in Chapter 2, once you can switch characters.","hidden":false,"id":34,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Retail Therapy","sources":[{"name":"GTABase — GTA 6 Trophies & Achievements Guide","url":"https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-achievements-trophies-list-ps5-xbox-series"},{"name":"gtasix.how — GTA 6 Trophies and Achievements","url":"https://gtasix.how/trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Finish Coffee Break in Chapter 2 so you can switch characters","With your partner, rob 3 shops in a row while still wanted","Use the jewelry stores in north Vice City; they sit close together","If it does not pop after the third, rob a fourth"]},
{"description":"Discover 100 vehicles.","grade":"bronze","guide":"You discover a vehicle automatically when you get inside one or scan one. A hundred different vehicles sounds like a lot, but it happens naturally through the story as you drive, steal and scan your way around Leonida. Keep track of what you have found with Touch Pad, then Progress, then Vehicles, and hop into anything new you see.","hidden":false,"id":35,"kind":"collectibles","missable":false,"name":"Whip It Good","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Get inside or scan 100 different vehicles","Track them: Touch Pad, then Progress, then Vehicles"]},
{"description":"Take down 5 enemies in a single use of Combat Focus.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Combat Focus slows time and lets you pick targets fast. Get into a fight with at least five enemies close together, trigger Combat Focus, and drop all five before it runs out. Crowded shootouts and gang hideouts are the easiest places to set it up: soften the group first, then trigger Focus and finish them.","hidden":false,"id":36,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Gunslinger","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Find a fight with at least 5 enemies close together","Trigger Combat Focus and take down all 5 before it ends"]},
{"description":"Make an unscheduled departure at VCIA.","grade":"bronze","guide":"At Vice City International Airport, steal a large passenger plane docked at a boarding bridge: the planes at gates E3 and E4 work, while planes parked elsewhere on the airfield do not count. Climb to the cockpit, back out toward the runway and take off. The trophy is delayed, so fly about 1 km away from the airport before it pops. Save first, because the police come fast.","hidden":true,"id":37,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Catch Me If You Can","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"egamers.io — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://egamers.io/gta-6-trophy-list-all-55-trophies-and-achievements-plus-the-hardest-ones/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Go to VCIA and find a docked passenger jet at gate E3 or E4","Steal it, back out to the runway and take off","Fly about 1 km away from the airport; the trophy pops delayed","Save first: the police come fast"]},
{"description":"Kinda hot in these Rhinos.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Steal a Rhino military tank from Mile Zero Air Station and take out enemies from inside it. The tank itself is the hard part: the air station is guarded, so go in fast, grab the Rhino and get moving, then use its cannon on the enemies that come after you. Once you have scored kills from inside the tank, the trophy pops.","hidden":true,"id":38,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Challenging Tank","sources":[{"name":"egamers.io — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://egamers.io/gta-6-trophy-list-all-55-trophies-and-achievements-plus-the-hardest-ones/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Get into Mile Zero Air Station and steal a Rhino tank","Take out enemies from inside the tank"]},
{"description":"Rob a jewelry store without being detected.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Pick a jewelry store, go in quiet, and take the goods without any guard or camera spotting you. Move slowly, stay out of sight lines, and leave the same way you came in: the trophy only counts if nobody detects you at any point. If you are spotted, walk away and try another store.","hidden":false,"id":39,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Sneakthief","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Pick a jewelry store and go in quiet","Take the goods without being detected by anyone","Leave without being spotted"]},
{"description":"Rob 5 Bank Vaults and escape.","grade":"silver","guide":"Rob five bank vaults and escape each time. Bank vault robberies always bring a 4-star Wanted Level, so they pair well with Hot Together: get the vault, get out, and lose the heat. Each vault counts once you have escaped cleanly, so plan your getaway before you go in.","hidden":false,"id":40,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Maximum Withdrawal","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"GTABase — GTA 6 Trophies & Achievements Guide","url":"https://www.gtabase.com/articles/gta-6/gta-6-achievements-trophies-list-ps5-xbox-series"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Rob a bank vault and escape; repeat for 5 vaults","Plan your getaway first: vaults always bring 4 stars"]},
{"description":"Rob an Armored Truck and escape.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Find an armored truck on the road, stop it, crack it open and take the cash, then escape. Trucks run set routes around the state, so watch for them while you drive. Once the money is yours, lose the police and the trophy pops.","hidden":false,"id":41,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"A Classic Blitz Play","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Find an armored truck on the road and stop it","Take the cash, then escape the police"]},
{"description":"Explore all of Leonida.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Explore every corner of the state of Leonida, from Vice City to the swamps of Mount Kalaga and the keys. The trophy tracks the areas you have visited, so drive, fly and sail into every region rather than sticking to the city. Exploring also feeds the other trophies: stunts, meditation spots, card sets and WAiNK locations are all out there waiting.","hidden":false,"id":42,"kind":"collectibles","missable":false,"name":"The Goodtime State","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Visit every region of Leonida, not just Vice City","Drive, fly and sail into new areas until the map is covered"]},
{"description":"Rob an Illegal Operation belonging to each gang.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Rob an illegal operation belonging to each of the nine gangs in Leonida. There are 39 operations in total, and the 100% checklist wants all of them, so this trophy pops on the way to full completion. Hit one operation per gang first to bank this trophy early, then keep going for the rest.","hidden":false,"id":43,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Pest Control","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Rob one illegal operation from each of the nine gangs","Keep going: all 39 operations count toward 100%"]},
{"description":"Enjoy a cocktail with a view on Ocean Beach.","grade":"bronze","guide":"The description is the whole hint: find a spot on Ocean Beach with a view, order a cocktail and enjoy it. No confirmed method has been published at launch, so treat this as an unconfirmed one: head to the beachfront bars on Ocean Drive, look for a drink prompt with a view, and try the spots that face the ocean. If nothing pops, come back once more of the map's tricks are known.","hidden":true,"id":44,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"In The Beginning…","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Head to the beachfront bars on Ocean Beach","Look for a cocktail prompt at a spot with a view","Unconfirmed at launch: try the ocean-facing spots first"]},
{"description":"Smash your way out of a vehicle showroom in classic style.","grade":"bronze","guide":"The description points at a classic GTA moment: driving a car straight through a vehicle showroom's glass and out the other side. No confirmed method has been published at launch, so the honest advice is to try it at a showroom with a car fast enough to smash through the front: drive in, floor it, and crash out through the glass. If it does not pop, come back once the method is confirmed.","hidden":true,"id":45,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Capital Offense","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Take a fast car to a vehicle showroom","Smash through the showroom glass and out the other side","Unconfirmed at launch: the showroom drive-through is the classic move"]},
{"description":"Follow-through at the Kolt & Associates' bowling alley.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Go to the Kolt & Associates bowling alley and play a game of bowling through to the end: follow-through means finishing what you start, so bowl the full game. Bowling is one of the activities around Vice City, and the alley is the named one, so this is the place to do it.","hidden":true,"id":46,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Let’s Go Bowling","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Go to the Kolt & Associates bowling alley","Bowl a full game through to the end"]},
{"description":"A partnership with mass appeal.","grade":"bronze","guide":"The description is cryptic, and no confirmed method has been published at launch. The name and the wording point at a moment with your partner that the public notices: a partnership played out where people can see it. Keep playing the partner missions and public moments as they come, and come back once players have pinned the exact trigger down.","hidden":true,"id":47,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Personal Best","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Play the partner missions and public moments as they come","Unconfirmed at launch: the exact trigger is not pinned down yet"]},
{"description":"Choices made (for better or worse).","grade":"bronze","guide":"The description points at the game's choices: somewhere in the story or the world you make a call, and this trophy marks it. No confirmed method has been published at launch, so the honest advice is to keep playing and watch for choice moments, especially in stranger missions and story beats where the game asks you to pick a side. It will come as you play the story through.","hidden":true,"id":48,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Actions Speak Louder","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":2,"steps":["Play the story and stranger missions through","Watch for moments where the game asks you to choose","Unconfirmed at launch: the exact choice is not pinned down yet"]},
{"description":"Second time's the charm.","grade":"bronze","guide":"The name says it: something that fails the first time works on the second try. No confirmed method has been published at launch, so this one is honest guesswork from the wording: when something in the game goes wrong on your first attempt, try it again right away instead of walking off. It is the kind of trophy that pops on its own while you play.","hidden":true,"id":49,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Bad Luck, I Guess","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["When something fails on the first try, try it again right away","Unconfirmed at launch: it likely pops on its own while you play"]},
{"description":"What the hell just happened?","grade":"bronze","guide":"The description is the reaction to something strange in the world, and no confirmed method has been published at launch. It reads like a random world event or an easter egg: keep your eyes open while you explore, especially in the odd corners of Leonida, and it will find you. This is one to leave until the cleanup, when players have mapped where the strange thing happens.","hidden":true,"id":50,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"The Truth Is Out There","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":5,"steps":["Explore the odd corners of Leonida and watch for strange events","Unconfirmed at launch: leave it for the cleanup once players map it"]},
{"description":"Bowl 'em over with a melee drive-by.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Knock someone down with a melee attack from a moving vehicle, a drive-by done with a bat or a fist instead of a gun. No confirmed method has been published at launch, but the wording is clear enough: get a vehicle moving, lean out with a melee weapon, and bowl someone over. Try it on a quiet road where you can line the hit up.","hidden":true,"id":51,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Ten Pin","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"planetgta6 — GTA 6 Trophies","url":"https://www.planetgta6.com/en/gta-6-trophies/"}],"stage":3,"steps":["Get a vehicle moving with a melee weapon ready","Lean out and bowl someone over with a melee drive-by","Unconfirmed at launch: a quiet road makes the hit easier to line up"]},
{"description":"Earn $250,000 laundering Marked Bills through your contacts.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Marked Bills come from bank and payday loan jobs; launder them by selling them to your contacts, and the $250,000 total is cumulative, so it builds up over the whole game. One fence pays the most, so once you find the best-paying contact, use them every time. The total grows naturally during the 100% robberies, so do not grind it early: let it come as you play.","hidden":false,"id":52,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Dime on the Dollar","sources":[{"name":"Output Lag — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://outputlag.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-list/"},{"name":"egamers.io — GTA 6 Trophy List","url":"https://egamers.io/gta-6-trophy-list-all-55-trophies-and-achievements-plus-the-hardest-ones/"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Earn Marked Bills from bank and payday loan jobs","Launder them through your contacts; the $250,000 total is cumulative","Use the best-paying fence once you find them"]},
{"description":"Spend $100,000 across all shops.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Simply spend $100,000 in total across the game's shops: clothes, weapons, food, whatever you like. It is the easiest money trophy in the game, and it counts every dollar you spend while playing. Find shops on the map with Touch Pad, then Style. By the time you have bought your garages and upgraded your cars, this one is usually done.","hidden":false,"id":53,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Treat Yo Self","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Spend $100,000 in total across any shops","Find shops with Touch Pad, then Style"]},
{"description":"Purchase all garage properties.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Buy all 8 garages through the Vice City Real Estate app on your phone (press Up to open it). They cost $160,000 in total: Mitchel Auto Center $4,000, 7th Avenue Garage $12,000, Vela Rota Drive Garage $24,000, Persistence Road Garage $7,600, Wyatt Motors $21,600, Bonita Court Garage $34,000, Atlantic Court Garage $40,000, and Store n' Bolt $16,800. Each gives you one parking spot, so your registered vehicles are saved for later and can be called with Scooter Bros.","hidden":false,"id":54,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"Little Boxes","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Open the Vice City Real Estate app on your phone (press Up)","Buy all 8 garages: $160,000 in total","Each garage adds one parking spot for registered vehicles"]},
{"description":"Register 10 vehicles to the Scooter Bros app.","grade":"bronze","guide":"Scooter Bros is the service that delivers your fully repaired, registered vehicles to your current location for a small fee. Register any vehicle you are driving at a Pay 'N' Spray or Mod Shop, as long as you have an empty parking spot; the fee varies with the vehicle's value. Register 10 different vehicles and the trophy pops. Buy more garages from the Vice City Real Estate app if you run out of parking spots.","hidden":false,"id":55,"kind":"activities","missable":false,"name":"On the Spot","sources":[{"name":"Push Square — GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","url":"https://www.pushsquare.com/guides/gta-6-trophy-guide-and-roadmap"}],"stage":4,"steps":["Drive a vehicle to a Pay 'N' Spray or Mod Shop","Register it to the Scooter Bros app","Repeat for 10 different vehicles; buy garages for more spots"]}]}
